{
  "question_id": "q_076_prime_warehouse_storage",
  "slug": "prime-warehouse-storage",
  "title": "Maximize Prime Item Inventory",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "Amazon",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "Amazon Fulfillment Operations needs to organize inventory storage inside a 500,000 square-foot warehouse facility.\n\nProducts arrive in fixed batch sets. To uphold fast delivery commitments, warehouse protocol mandates **prioritizing Prime-eligible product batches first**:\n1. Stock as many complete Prime product batches as possible into the 500,000 sq ft facility.\n2. Allocate any remaining square footage to stock as many complete non-Prime batches as possible.\n\nWrite a query to calculate the maximum number of items of each type (`item_type` is `'prime_eligible'` or `'not_prime'`) that can be stocked. Output `item_type` and `item_count`, where `item_count` is the total number of items across all the batches stocked.",
  "notes": [
    "Prioritize stocking prime batches",
    "After accommodating prime items, allocate any remaining space to non-prime batches",
    "Again, products must be stocked in batches, so we want to find the largest available quantity of prime batches, and then the largest available quantity of non-prime batches",
    "Non-prime items must always be available in stock to meet customer demand, so the non-prime item count should never be zero.",
    "Item count should be whole numbers (integers)."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "inventory",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "item_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "item_type",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "item_category",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "square_footage",
          "data_type": "DECIMAL(10,2)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "inventory": [
      {
        "item_id": "1374",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "mini refrigerator",
        "square_footage": "68.00"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "4245",
        "item_type": "not_prime",
        "item_category": "standing lamp",
        "square_footage": "26.40"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "2452",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "television",
        "square_footage": "85.00"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "3255",
        "item_type": "not_prime",
        "item_category": "side table",
        "square_footage": "22.60"
      },
      {
        "item_id": "1672",
        "item_type": "prime_eligible",
        "item_category": "laptop",
        "square_footage": "8.50"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "item_type": "prime_eligible",
      "item_count": 9285
    },
    {
      "item_type": "not_prime",
      "item_count": 6
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "WITH summary AS (\n  SELECT \n    item_type,\n    SUM(square_footage) AS total_sqft,\n    COUNT(item_id) AS item_count\n  FROM inventory\n  GROUP BY item_type\n),\nprime_calc AS (\n  SELECT \n    'prime_eligible' AS item_type,\n    FLOOR(500000 / total_sqft) * item_count AS item_count,\n    FLOOR(500000 / total_sqft) * total_sqft AS total_sqft_used\n  FROM summary\n  WHERE item_type = 'prime_eligible'\n),\nnot_prime_calc AS (\n  SELECT \n    'not_prime' AS item_type,\n    FLOOR((500000 - p.total_sqft_used) / s.total_sqft) * s.item_count AS item_count\n  FROM summary s\n  CROSS JOIN prime_calc p\n  WHERE s.item_type = 'not_prime'\n)\nSELECT item_type, item_count FROM prime_calc\nUNION ALL\nSELECT item_type, item_count FROM not_prime_calc;",
  "tags": [
    "aggregation",
    "amazon",
    "date-manipulation",
    "ecommerce",
    "finance",
    "hard"
  ],
